  "open_questions": [
   "This record's own geometry file states the building's name/address/operator are not confirmed by any source checked in the geometry-correction pass. This research pass found a strong but not fully confirmed candidate: UCSF's Bayfront Medical Building (520 Illinois St), the clinical half of the 'Block 34 Clinical Building and Parking Garage' project, whose own CEQA filing places it south of the Wayne and Gladys Valley Center for Vision (this project's mission_bay_490_illinois record) and at the corner of 3rd and Mariposa -- matching this record's own notes exactly (south building, extending to Mariposa St). No source directly ties an address to this record's own OCII plan-block-34 parcel number, so the identification is geographic inference from UCSF's own project descriptions, not confirmed by an address-to-parcel source.",
   "Exact opening day within August 2024 is inconsistent across sources found (a UCSF news article dated 2024-08 vs. secondary reports of an August 23 opening event and an August 27 first-patients date); not resolved here, only the month is used.",
   "Total project cost is reported elsewhere as approximately $335.8 million for the combined clinical building and garage; not broken out per building and not independently verified against a primary UCSF or Regents document in this pass, so left out of costs."
  ],
